            [decided: agent 2026-11-16] the lane and incarnation setters note every change, so a step writes all it
            touched; putting a head on the wire (sendLane) is the one unnoted move, since its batch already holds it in
            flight. Why: a write per send doubled batches for no new bytes. Reverse: per-move saves.
        comment     2026-11-16T09:14:34Z
            Decision (agent, 2026-11-16): a Recapturing head's lane record carries retryCount + 1 while memory keeps the
            invoked count, so a refused capture needs no undo; a refused batch goes again after 5 s whatever captureMs
            is, so captureMs 0 never loops on a refusing store. Reverse: raise the count at Recapturing, undo
            on refusal.
