    T81
        title           Construction decodes whole: one config Schema, Flow-made values by identity, builders that
                        capture
        status          tombstone
        priority        high
        blocked_by      [@T82, @T94]
        description
            `definition()` and `machine()` accept a value only after one complete Schema decode, trust a Flow-made value
            only by identity, and refuse everything else with a FlowError.

            **Why now:** T81 hit the failure limit (V3.log, 2026-11-18T11:22) on three blockers of the raw-throw class:
            (1) a handle's call arguments are read before any check (`O.save.retryable(undefined)` throws in the body,
            `retryable(5)` is accepted); (2) `machine()` trusts its definition by the copyable `~owner` mark (`machine({
            "~owner": Symbol() })` throws raw); (3) a cyclic or throwing value inside the config escapes as Effect's
            adapter error, because `findingsAgainst` (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/config.ts) runs Effect's parser
            rather than the cycle-safe walker. Each review found the next hole because tokens are checked by shape,
            builders read early, and the decode is not the walker. Rebuilt on the boundary Task's catch-all (the user,
            2026-11-18, re-plan Q1 B); construction only.

            **Read first:** this Task's requirements 1 to 19 and its 2026-11-18T11:21:42Z review below, @spec.Compile,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/config.ts, @convention.boundaries.

            **Risk:** the `WeakSet` check makes a token from a second copy of the package foreign; one package copy per
            app is already assumed (one Effect copy since T93).

            **Approach:** first, the three blockers land as known-gap tests (`it.fails`, red for their stated reason).
            Then, in order:

            - `src/made.ts`: one module `WeakSet` of definitions and machines Flow made, and one `WeakSet` per
              definition of its tokens (states, events, guards, actions, entries, handles' calls). `machine()` checks
              membership; a guard, action or event is foreign when its definition's set lacks it. `~owner`, `~flow`,
              `HandleId` and `decodedWhole` are deleted.
            - Builders capture: `retryable`, `commit`, `idle`, `lookup`, `resource`, `transaction`, `.outcomes`,
              `Flow.initial` and `actorRef` store their arguments unread; the `definition` or `machine` decode checks
              them, so `retryable(5)` is `WrongKind` at its path.
            - One complete Schema per entry (`DefinitionArgs`, `MachineArgs`), decoded through `walkerOf`, so a cycle or
              a throwing getter is a finding with its cause; the decoded value, branded with `Schema.brand`, is the one
              internals take, and the casts and `trusted<T>()` that the discarded value forced go away.

            The per-definition type brand on tokens (ruling c) is not built: moved to revisit.md (the user, 2026-11-18,
            Q3 A); the run-time ForeignToken refusal stands.

            May change: `src/`, `tests/`, `fixtures/`, @spec.Compile and @spec.Diagnostics with `specs.log` notes.
            Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a decode that still accepts by shape (a partial token, a copied definition) → caught by the
            boundary Task's hostile-value table, which includes copied and partial tokens at every position. Gates: `nub
            run faults --only` on its planted faults `token-by-shape` (membership check skipped), `builder-reads-early`
            (`retryable` reads `times`) and `decode-not-walker` (Effect's parser restored), each caught by its named
            test. User's read: each new refusal code or path.
        acceptance
            - The three blockers are red first as known-gap tests, each for its stated reason, then green.
            - Requirements 1 to 19 (this Task's comments) stay green; every refusal is a FlowError with a code from
              Diagnostics' list.
            - No `~owner`, `~flow` or `HandleId` remains in `src/`; Flow-made values are checked by `WeakSet`
              membership only.
            - No builder reads its arguments: a test calls each with a Proxy that throws on every trap and gets a value.
            - `definition` and `machine` decode through `walkerOf` with one Schema each; the decoded value is used.
            - `nub run check`, the suite and stress pass; `nub run faults --only` catches this Task's planted faults.
        comment         2026-11-16T15:07:48Z
            Decided by the orchestrator (user-delegated, 2026-11-16): split the test that expects a duplicate state name
            beside a wrong-kind state; with one decode, list-wide rules run once items decode, and Compile R2 asks only
            for what construction finds.
        comment         2026-11-16T15:37:32Z
