    T94
        title       Every public entry point refuses with a FlowError; a surface test finds any that doesn't
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            Every public function Flow exports or hands out either refuses with a FlowError or is an inert builder, and
            a test proves it without a hand-kept list.

            **Why now:** T81's last three blockers and the routed raw throws (`app`, `runtimeSetup`, `actorRef`,
            `createActor`, `ensureActor`, `disposeActor`, `resource`, `transaction`, `send` with a throwing getter) are
            one class: no public function has a catch-all, so anything a check missed escapes as a raw TypeError. The
            corruption sweep (`tests/compile/corruption.test.ts`) lists its slots by hand, which is how T81's blockers 1
            and 2 were missed. Also from @task.V3.T80 (its 2026-11-17T13:23:59Z comment): a throw from `perform` or the
            admit hook skips the rest of the step's commands while the Runtime stays Open
            (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/driver.ts); it must stop the Runtime as Actors R25 does.

            **Read first:** @convention.boundaries, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/boundary.ts#walkerOf,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/compile/corruption.test.ts, @spec.Diagnostics; the re-plan's section
            2, @proposal.replan.

            **Approach:** `src/entry.ts` exports `entry(name, run)` for sync calls and `entryEffect(name, run)` for
            Effect-returning ones (`ready`, `dispose`), whose refusal is `Effect.fail` (Diagnostics R1). Each wraps
            `run` in `Result.try`; a FlowError passes through, anything else is `Defect` at `name` with the cause. Every
            public function goes through one, or is registered as a builder. The surface test builds every fixture app's
            definitions, machines, app, Runtime and one actor, walks every function-valued property reachable from them
            and from `src/index.ts`, and requires each to be a registered entry or builder, naming the path of any
            other. A hostile-value table (null, undefined, NaN, ±Infinity, a Date, a Map, a function, a cycle, a
            throwing getter, a Proxy that throws on every trap, a copied token) runs at every argument position of every
            entry; each call returns or throws a FlowError, under a 1 s bound. The driver's stray throw stops the
            Runtime (Actors R25), red first.

            May change: `src/`, `tests/`, `tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md`, `vite.config.ts` (lint), `wiki/conventions/`,
            @spec.Diagnostics with a `specs.log` note. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: an entry point the walk can't reach (a function only a callback receives) → caught by the walk
            also visiting the arguments Flow passes to body and operations callbacks (`S`, `E`, `O`). Gates: `nub run
            faults --only` on its planted faults `entry-unwrapped` (one export loses its wrapper), `stray-throw-raw`
            (the wrapper rethrows the cause) and `driver-throw-stays-open`, each caught by its named test. User's read:
            the list of functions registered as builders, and any entry point given a new refusal code.
        acceptance
            - The surface test passes on every fixture app, and fails naming the path when one export's wrapper
              is removed.
            - Every hostile value at every argument position of every entry gives a FlowError or a normal return; no raw
              error and no hang.
            - Lint: `hasProperty(_, "~` is banned in `src/`; `throw` outside `src/error.ts`, `src/entry.ts` and the
              core's listed defect sites is flagged; each remaining disable carries its reason.
            - A throw from `perform` or the admit hook stops the Runtime (Actors R25), shown red first by a Story test.
            - @convention.boundaries stays current: any source this Task adds or moves changes its row.
            - `nub run check`, the suite and stress pass; `nub run faults --only` catches this Task's planted faults.
        comment     2026-11-18T18:28:19Z
            [decided: agent 2026-11-18] the surface walk follows own enumerable keys, stops at Flow's inert data (a
            builder's result, Compiled, a bound contract, a walker) and Effect's own values, and treats a builder as a
            leaf; only the root route and what it hands out are walked, not the testing route. Why: user callbacks live
            only inside that data. Reverse: enter inert data and register user callbacks.
