    T101
        title       P3's coverage gaps closed: each built rule caught by a named fault
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            Every Spec rule P3 built has a test that fails on a named planted fault, so P3's exit criterion holds.

            **Why now:** P3's completion audit can't pass: its coverage record lists 58 rules with no catching fault (37
            tested, 21 with no test citing them). Deferring them would relax a gate, which is the user's call, so this
            Task closes them instead.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/tasks/V3/P3-coverage.md ("Gaps"), code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts and
            the files it spreads, @phase.V3.P3 (its exit criteria).

            **Approach:** for each gap rule, first decide whether P3 built it: read the code it governs.

            - Built: plant one named fault citing the rule (in the matching `tests/*-faults.ts`), and make sure a test
              titled by the rule catches it: an existing test if it already does, else a new test written from the Spec
              rule, red on the plant. A rule a fault can't express (a type rule, a pure naming rule) is shown by a
              compile-time test or a lint plant instead, with the reason.
            - Not built (its code belongs to a later Task, such as Diagnostics R10's renderer): not a P3 gap; record it
              on its owner Task and move it out of P3's gaps.
            - A plant the tests miss because the runtime is wrong is a found bug: an `it.fails` test titled by its rule,
              with its owner Task.

            Then update the coverage record so each rule is caught, moved out, or an inverted test.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, `packages/flow-state-v3/src/` only to make a plant's target
            text unique, code:wiki/tasks/V3/P3-coverage.md. Evidence: this Task's comments and the coverage record.

            False pass: a fault that edits code no test reaches, counted as caught → caught by `nub run faults --only
            <names>` reporting each new fault caught by a named test.
        acceptance
            - Each of the 58 gap rules in code:wiki/tasks/V3/P3-coverage.md is caught by a named fault, moved to its
              owner Task as not built in P3 (with evidence), or held as an `it.fails` test with an owner.
            - `nub run faults --only <the new faults>` catches each by a named test.
            - The coverage record is updated and lists no unexplained gap.
            - `nub run check`, the suite and stress pass.
